# 0013. Feed sources: Jobicy, Remote OK, Remotive and Dev Global Jobs, closed after 30 days unseen

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-14

Four remote-job feeds from `docs/sources.json` become source kinds. Unlike company boards,
they list only recent jobs, so "missing from the list" cannot mean "closed". This ADR decides
how such postings close, how their attribution terms are met, and how Remotive's request
limit is enforced.

## Technical details

**Problem.** ADR 0005 closes a posting when a complete listing no longer has it. These feeds
are a window of recent jobs (Remote OK ~100, Jobicy ≤100, Remotive ~16 and delayed 24h, Dev
Global Jobs paged over ~112k): a job drops out while still open. Treated as truncated
(`ErrTruncated`), nothing would ever close them.

**Kinds and what a source row means** (like Himalayas: a row is a saved feed filter):

| kind | endpoint | board_token | config |
|---|---|---|---|
| `jobicy` | `GET https://jobicy.com/api/jobs?count=100`, cursor pages over a 7-day window | `tag` (e.g. `data engineer`), or `all` | `geo`, `industry` |
| `remoteok` | `GET https://remoteok.com/api` (`?tag=`) | `tag` (e.g. `data`), or `all` | none |
| `remotive` | `GET https://remotive.com/api/remote-jobs` | `search` term, or `all` | `category` |
| `devglobaljobs` | `GET https://devglobaljobs.com/api/v1/jobs` (offset/limit), then `/api/v1/jobs/{id}` per job (the list has only an excerpt) | `search` term, or `all` | `category`, `country`; the newest 200 jobs per sync (a window, like the others) |

Parameters, terms and data notes are in each package doc (`internal/ingest/{jobicy,remoteok,
remotive,devglobaljobs}`), with a trimmed real response in `testdata/`. Checked live on
2026-11-14: Jobicy and Remotive return their whole feed whatever the keyword, so a keyword
narrows little there; filters (`geo`, `industry`, `category`) do. A config key outside each
kind's list is refused when the source is created (`ingest.FeedParams`).

**Closing: 30 days unseen.** An optional interface in `internal/ingest` (`feed.go`):
```go
// FeedAdapter lists only recent jobs: its fetch is never complete, and a posting closes
// once no sync has seen it for StaleAfter.
type FeedAdapter interface { StaleAfter() time.Duration }
```
For a feed adapter the sync skips the "missing" rule and instead calls the existing
`ClosePostingsNotSeenSince` with `run start - StaleAfter()` (30 days for all four,
`ingest.FeedStaleAfter`), when every posting was stored. No new query or migration for this.
A posting seen again reopens its job, as today. A feed run that works is `succeeded`, not
`partial`.
- *Changed during implementation (2026-11-14):* the approved draft had feed adapters return
  `ErrTruncated`. That would make every feed run `partial`, and the scheduler re-runs any
  source without a recent `succeeded` run on every tick (`ListDueSources`): Remotive would
  be called far beyond its terms. The sync recognises `FeedAdapter` instead; the behaviour
  (never close as missing, close after 30 days unseen) is the same.

**Attribution (terms).** `sources[].attribution` in `/api/v1/jobs` (ADR 0011) moves from a
Himalayas special case to a per-kind map in `internal/api/jobs.go`:
`himalayas` "via Himalayas", `jobicy` "via Jobicy", `remoteok` "via Remote OK", `remotive`
"via Remotive", `devglobaljobs` "via Dev Global Jobs". The job URL stays the feed's own URL
(each feed requires linking back to it). jobradar-web already shows `attribution` next to
the link; it also gets a footer "Powered by Dev Global Jobs" linking https://devglobaljobs.com
(its license asks for that visible link). Links stay followed (no `nofollow`: Remote OK).
None of these jobs leave the app (Remotive and Himalayas forbid passing them on).

**Request limits.** Optional interface `MinInterval() time.Duration`: Remotive returns 6h
(its terms: at most 4 requests a day), Jobicy 1h (at most hourly). `SyncLocked` checks it under
the source's lock against the last run's start, whatever that run's outcome, so the scheduler
skips such a source quietly, and a manual `POST /sources/{id}/sync` inside the window gets 429
with `Retry-After`. Remotive's client also retries at most once. Each adapter gets its own
slow HTTP client, as Himalayas does.

**Data.** Jobicy, Remote OK and Remotive are remote boards: `remote_policy` is `remote`. Dev
Global Jobs is a global board (found live): `remote` only when its `country` is "Remote",
otherwise `unknown`; an ISO `country` fills `countries`. Salary only from structured
fields (Jobicy `salaryMin/Max/Currency/Period`; Remote OK `salary_min/max`, USD per year,
kept only within 1,000-2,000,000 because the feed carries values like 21); none parsed from
text (ADR 0005). Remote OK's element 0 is its legal notice and is skipped.

**Migration** `00008_feed_sources.sql`: replace the `sources.kind` CHECK to add the four
kinds; the API's `sourceKinds` filter list grows to match.

**Consequences.**
- Dedup (ADR 0005, company + title + location) links the same job seen on several feeds and
  boards; its `sources` list shows all of them.
- A closed job may stay open up to 30 days after it really closed; applying shows it.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: stdlib `net/http` and `encoding/json`, the existing `ingest.HTTPClient`; no new dependency.
- Alternatives:
  - `ErrTruncated` only: feed jobs never close.
  - Close when missing from one fetch: closes open jobs every day.
  - Probe each job URL for 404: one request per job per sync, against the feeds' rate terms.
  - Set `expires_at = now + 30d` on fetch: unchanged postings skip that update (`TouchPosting`), so it needs the same sync change anyway.
